SET1, 1310, 97, 98, 99, 100, 111, 112, 121, 122, 211,
+, 212, 221, 222
AECOMP, ALLGRID, SET1, 1310
$ Whole-aircraft aero boxes (all 4 CAERO1 panels)
AELIST, 1400, 1000, THRU, 1007, 1100, THRU, 1131, 2000, THRU, 2007, 2100, THRU, 2131
AECOMP, ALLAERO, AELIST, 1400
$ MONPNT3 section cuts (aero + inertia + reaction) and MONPNT1 aero-only:
MONPNT3, MWINGRT, WING ROOT, 35, WINGROOT, 0, 15.0, 0.0, 0.0
MONPNT3, MWINGEA, RIGHT WING, 35, WINGEA, 0, 15.0, 0.0, 0.0
MONPNT3, MALLEA, WHOLE AIRCRAFT, 35, ALLGRID, 0, 15.0, 0.0, 0.0
MONPNT1, MALLAR, AIRCRAFT AERO, 35, ALLAERO, 0, 15.0, 0.0, 0.0
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------
$ SECTION-CUT RUNNING LOADS (MONSECT, Monitor Phase 2 / V-SEC)
$ ------------------------------------------------------------
$ CID 2 is the RIGHT wing SPLINE2 axis, reused verbatim as the cut frame — its
$ y-axis is the swept elastic axis through GRIDs 100/110/120, so the default
$ AXIS=2 measures stations along the EA and every cut's moment reference lands
$ on it.  Cut planes are normal to the EA, so the two stringers at one y land at
$ different stations (112 at 4.52, 111 at 7.02; 122 at 16.07, 121 at 18.57).
$ Collection: every RIGHT-wing grid that carries aero load or mass.
SET1, 1330, 111, 112, 121, 122
AECOMP, RWINGALL, SET1, 1330
$ Stations 8/10 cut ONLY CBAR 120 (EA nodes at 5.77 and 11.55, stringers at
$ 4.52/7.02 inboard and 16.07/18.57 outboard) — the free-body identity against
$ the element internal force (V-SEC2).  12 also crosses the tip RBARs; 20 is
$ outboard of everything and must return exactly zero (V-SEC4).
MONSECT, SECRW, RIGHT WING EA, RWINGALL, 2
+, 8.0, 10.0, 12.0, 20.0
